---
import Layout from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Who writes zhao-langxi, why these human-robot interaction questions matter, how evidence is labelled, and where to find professional work."
  canonical="https://zhao-langxi.github.io/zhao-langxi/about.html"
  current="about"
>
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <header>
      <div>
        <p>About this publication</p>
        <h1>Jade Zhao · <span lang="zh-Hans">赵郎溪</span></h1>
      </div>
      <div>
        <img alt="Jade Zhao, profile photo." class="author-avatar" decoding="async" height="120" src={`${base}assets/site-pfp.jpg`} width="120" />
      </div>
    </header>
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Who writes</h2>
      <p>
        Jade Zhao. Informatics student at Indiana University. I write from human-centred design and technology, not as a robotics engineer.
        <span lang="zh-Hans">赵郎溪</span> is an independent essay publication, not Indiana University research and not peer-reviewed work.
      </p>
      <h2>Why these questions</h2>
      <p>
        Intelligent systems are entering shared life: screens that speak like people, tools that filter choices, institutions that catalogue “digital humans.”
        This publication asks what that means for trust, interruption, accessibility, and agency ... especially after the demo ends.
      </p>
      <h2>How evidence is handled</h2>
      <p>
        Essays use four labels: <strong>Observed</strong>, <strong>Reported</strong>, <strong>Interpreted</strong>, and <strong>Open question</strong>.
        I do not claim fieldwork I did not do. Public catalogues and media coverage are evidence of what institutions publish, not proof that people trust or use a system well.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={`${base}research/evidence-labels.md`}>Read the evidence labels</a> ·
        <a href={`${base}research.html`}>Research hub</a>
      </p>
      <h2>Where professional work lives</h2>
      <p>
        Case studies, code, and employment detail belong on
        <a href="https://jadexzhao.github.io/jadexzhao/" rel="noopener noreferrer">jadexzhao</a>.
        Coursework and handoff guides belong on
        <a href="https://matchaxmoxie.github.io/matchaxmoxie/" rel="noopener noreferrer">matchaxmoxie</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://jadexzhao.github.io/jadexzhao/resume.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer">Résumé (PDF)</a> ·
        <a href="mailto:jlzhao@iu.edu">jlzhao@iu.edu</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
